{
  "case_id": "2006-06-427",
  "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Tennessee Secondary School Athletic Association (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this Court adheres to its State action ruling, it should now hold that the TSSAA has broad discretion to adopt and to enforcement contractual restrictions on athletic recruiting as a condition of membership."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I ask you a preliminary question, Ms. Mahoney?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "TSSAA Rule",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "coach-initiated contact with students who are enrolled at another school is not supposed to occur."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The position of the United States is that the court of appeals applied the wrong standard in deciding Brentwood's First Amendment claim. This Court's decisions establish that when the government offers a benefit that a citizen is free to reject, it has much greater leeway in regulating speech than when it exercises its coercive sovereign power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Prohibiting the use of undue influence in recruiting or attempting to secure or retain high school athletes we think is self-evidently reasonable in light of the purposes underlying the rule, which include preventing the exploitation of children and ensuring that sports remains subordinate to academics."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this, what is your response to the, one of your earlier questions. Suppose they sent out a general brochure to all the graduating grammar school students to -- advertising that they come up to Brentwood and so forth and so on, and the rule prohibited that? Would that rule be valid?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I'm sorry; you think it might be a reasonable or unreasonable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: It seems to me that, turning to the state action for a moment, one of the justifications for finding state action that is there is no other real choice, that they have, other than to -- if they want to play athletics in Tennessee other than to join this association."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "James B. Blumstein (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BLUMSTEIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I represent Brentwood Academy in this civil rights case. It's about the regulatory overreaching of the Tennessee Secondary School Athletic Association, what we call the TSSAA. The case involves the First Amendment's interest of the school, its students, its parents, and the procedural due process interests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if the state set up two athletic leagues and one had an anti-recruiting rule and the other didn't, and they were equally strong, and you chose to join the one that had the anti-recruiting league. Would it be a violation of the First Amendment in your opinion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Blumstein (representing the Association)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, in this case, the association allows the underlying practice itself. It permits the underlying practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-427",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ef3713675d994e3e86c1e7aa43a2980d1abe137b6fe4a7b5ba82a09c462b3a19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ef3713675d99-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court found there was misleading of the school and that they -- the school never had a chance to respond to the evidence that was presented by these investigators for the association."
    },
